r600: big-endian query results (occlusion, time elapsed, timestamp, streamout, pipeline statistics)

The GPU writes the query results as little-endian dwords. The CPU read them
as host dwords, so on a big-endian host the "result written" bit (bit 63)
was never seen and every occlusion query counted 0 samples; timer queries
read byte-swapped times. Read the dwords as little-endian, and write the
bit for unused backends the same way. Found by piglit
(arb_occlusion_query, ext_timer_query) on a Power Mac G5;
tools/guest/occtest.c.

diff -ruN a/src/gallium/drivers/r600/r600_query.c b/src/gallium/drivers/r600/r600_query.c
